{"id":1739441,"retrievedAt":"2026-07-29T13:20:46.230Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/x0AxEGGBC45itsnnTjc1rfHwlA1.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":16,"name":"Animation"},{"id":10402,"name":"Music"}],"homepage":"","id":1739441,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["PL"],"original_language":"pl","original_title":"Mazurek","overview":"A film miniature to classical music by Fryderyk Chopin, Mazurka in A minor, Op. 17, No. 4, arranged and performed by Arnold Dąbrowski. A sentimental, romantic, and lyrical \" journey \" through Polish landscapes, like a memory recalled from somewhere beyond the fog. The image is in sepia. This subtle hue of an old photograph is only occasionally interrupted by a sudden burst of color, an intensified lushness of green, or a stronger accent of spot and line. The delicate horizon line evokes a graphic space of colorful checkerboard fields and meadows. We follow a leaf carried by the wind to admire the effect its shadow creates on the water. A sudden gust sends thousands of dandelions high into the air, creating a graphic procession that freezes for a moment, and just as suddenly as it appeared, it disappears. In its place, a butterfly swoops in. It enchants with a play of colors, shapes, and the shapes of its wings.","popularity":0.0786,"poster_path":"/gpX0gsf1kCTnKncPuMx8YZY7Mas.jpg","production_companies":[{"id":74640,"logo_path":null,"name":"Telewizyjne Studio Filmów Animowanych w Poznaniu","origin_country":"PL"},{"id":11240,"logo_path":"/i59ItaKFdxJ7Yi6w2s7CML0LBvI.png","name":"Polski Instytut Sztuki Filmowej","origin_country":"PL"}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"PL","name":"Poland"}],"release_date":"2010-04-15","revenue":0,"runtime":3,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"No Language","iso_639_1":"xx","name":"No Language"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"Mazurka","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[],"c